Here are the two precise replacements to fix the scrolling issue in the View modal and properly display the "No. of Entries" column.
### 1. Fix the Table Scroll (Add overflowY: "auto")
In your styles object at the top of the file, your tableContainer is missing the overflowY property, which means the table won't spawn a scrollbar when the rows exceed the maxHeight.
**Find this block (around line 38):**
```javascript
  tableContainer: { maxHeight: 500, border: 1, borderColor: "divider", mt: 1 },
  fixedContentBox: {
    height: 500,
    display: "flex",
    flexDirection: "column",
    justifyContent: "space-between",
  },

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
  tableContainer: { 
    maxHeight: 450, 
    overflowY: "auto", // Forces the vertical scrollbar to appear
    border: 1, 
    borderColor: "divider", 
    mt: 1 
  },
  fixedContentBox: {
    minHeight: 400, // Changed to minHeight for better responsiveness
    display: "flex",
    flexDirection: "column",
    justifyContent: "space-between",
  },

```
### 2. Increase Width for "No. of Entries"
Scroll down to your columns array definition (around line 350). The width is currently set to 100, which is truncating the text. We will increase it to 150 just like in the Authorization screen and remove the accidental leading space in the header name.
**Find this block:**
```javascript
    {
      field: "requestCount",
      headerName: " No. of Entries",
      width: 100,
      align: "center",
      headerAlign: "center",
      disableColumnMenu: true,
      sortable: false,
    },

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
    {
      field: "requestCount",
      headerName: "No. of Entries",
      width: 150, // Increased width to fully show the header text
      align: "center",
      headerAlign: "center",
      disableColumnMenu: true,
      sortable: false,
    },

```
